research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.findings.md-158-Proposed Fact replacement and proof branch:
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.findings.md-159-
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.findings.md-160-> `[L5] K is compact: from every family of open sets whose union contains K, either K = ∅ and the empty subfamily covers it, or there are m in N and members U_0,...,U_m of the family whose union contains K; compactness is equivalent to being closed and bounded ([[def-open-cover-r]], [[thm-heine-borel-characterisation-r]]).`
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.findings.md-161->
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.findings.md-162-> Before the current reverse-direction construction: `If K = ∅, then for every ε > 0 the single interval [0,0] covers K and has total length 0 ≤ ε, so K has content zero by [L1]. Hence suppose K ≠ ∅.` Then reflow the remaining steps.
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.findings.md-163-
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.findings.md-164-Under `K ≠ ∅`, the open cover in the current step 3.1 has a nonempty finite subcover, so the present finite-index estimate is valid. The new branch proves the omitted boundary directly from the cited content-zero definition.
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.findings.md-165-
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.findings.md:166:### 10. `lem-nondegenerate-interval-is-not-null` — class (b)
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.findings.md-167-
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.findings.md-168-Current Fact `[L4]` states compactness for every subset of `R` using only a nonempty list `U_0,...,U_m`, omitting the empty-set/empty-subfamily clause of `def-open-cover-r`. The proof’s actual use is safe because step 1.1 has already established `a < b`, so `[a,b]` is nonempty, but the Fact itself overstates its cited source.
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.findings.md-169-
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.findings.md-170-Proposed Fact replacement:
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.findings.md-171-
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.findings.md-172-> `[L4] A subset of R is compact exactly when it is closed and bounded ([[thm-heine-borel-characterisation-r]]); from every family of open sets whose union contains a compact set, either the set is empty and the empty subfamily covers it, or one can extract m in N and members U_0,...,U_m of the family whose union already contains it ([[def-open-cover-r]]).`
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.findings.md-173-
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.findings.md-174-No proof-step change is needed: step 1.1 licenses the nonempty branch before step 3.1 invokes compactness.
