research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cex-dense-set-of-measure-zero.md-907-intervals with the same lengths. The definition is therefore stated with closed
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cex-dense-set-of-measure-zero.md-908-intervals once and for all. Covers by *open* intervals are a genuinely different
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cex-dense-set-of-measure-zero.md-909-demand, and passing to one costs a little extra length: the enlargement
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cex-dense-set-of-measure-zero.md-910-$[a_k,b_k] \subseteq (a_k - \delta_k,\ b_k + \delta_k)$ is carried out where it is
