research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cex-null-set-not-of-content-zero.md-88-- **Boundedness is not what is missing.** $E$ is bounded, and its failure is as
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cex-null-set-not-of-content-zero.md-89-  large as it can be: no finite cover does better than the trivial cover of
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cex-null-set-not-of-content-zero.md-90-  $[0,1]$ by itself. What $E$ lacks is closedness, and hence compactness; adding
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cex-null-set-not-of-content-zero.md-91-  it repairs the implication completely ([[thm-compact-null-is-content-zero]]).
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cex-null-set-not-of-content-zero.md-92-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cex-null-set-not-of-content-zero.md-93-- **The closure is the whole obstruction.** Content zero is insensitive to
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cex-null-set-not-of-content-zero.md-94-  passing to the closure, since a finite union of closed intervals is closed,
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cex-null-set-not-of-content-zero.md-95-  whereas measure zero is not: $E$ is null and $\overline{E} = [0,1]$ is not
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cex-null-set-not-of-content-zero.md:96:  ([[lem-nondegenerate-interval-is-not-null]]). That single asymmetry is the
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cex-null-set-not-of-content-zero.md-97-  entire difference between the two notions.
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cex-null-set-not-of-content-zero.md-98-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cex-null-set-not-of-content-zero.md-99-- **Compare the compact case.** The Cantor set is uncountable and null, and being
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cex-null-set-not-of-content-zero.md-100-  compact it also has content zero ([[thm-cantor-set-properties]]). So the failure
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cex-null-set-not-of-content-zero.md-101-  here is not about cardinality: a much larger null set can have content zero,
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cex-null-set-not-of-content-zero.md-102-  and a countable one need not.
