research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-q-covered-by-intervals-of-small-total-length.md-1627-**Closed intervals lose nothing.** A bounded interval with endpoints
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-q-covered-by-intervals-of-small-total-length.md-1628-$a \le b$ is contained in $[a,b]$ and has the same length ([[def-interval]]), so
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-q-covered-by-intervals-of-small-total-length.md-1629-a cover by intervals of any of the four bounded forms yields a cover by closed
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-q-covered-by-intervals-of-small-total-length.md-1630-intervals with the same lengths. The definition is therefore stated with closed
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-q-covered-by-intervals-of-small-total-length.md-1631-intervals once and for all. Covers by *open* intervals are a genuinely different
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-q-covered-by-intervals-of-small-total-length.md-1632-demand, and passing to one costs a little extra length: the enlargement
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-q-covered-by-intervals-of-small-total-length.md-1633-$[a_k,b_k] \subseteq (a_k - \delta_k,\ b_k + \delta_k)$ is carried out where it is
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-q-covered-by-intervals-of-small-total-length.md:1634:needed, in [[lem-nondegenerate-interval-is-not-null]] and in
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-q-covered-by-intervals-of-small-total-length.md-1635-[[thm-compact-null-is-content-zero]].
