research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-q-covered-by-intervals-of-small-total-length.md-1638-then any cover of $A$ covers $B$, so $B$ is null; the same sentence with finite
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-q-covered-by-intervals-of-small-total-length.md-1639-covers shows a subset of a set of content zero has content zero.
