research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-q-covered-by-intervals-of-small-total-length.md-1659-  notion is the vanishing of the Lebesgue outer measure. Neither outer quantity
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-q-covered-by-intervals-of-small-total-length.md-1660-  is defined in this library, and no item here assigns a nonzero size to any set:
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-q-covered-by-intervals-of-small-total-length.md-1661-  every statement is of the shape "can, or cannot, be covered by intervals of
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-q-covered-by-intervals-of-small-total-length.md-1662-  total length below such and such a bound". That is a deliberate restriction of
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-q-covered-by-intervals-of-small-total-length.md-1663-  scope at this point in the reading order, not a claim that the general notions
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-q-covered-by-intervals-of-small-total-length.md-1664-  are unavailable in mathematics.
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-q-covered-by-intervals-of-small-total-length.md-1665-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-q-covered-by-intervals-of-small-total-length.md-1666-- **Measure zero is not vacuous and not universal.** No interval with two
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-q-covered-by-intervals-of-small-total-length.md:1667:  distinct endpoints is null ([[lem-nondegenerate-interval-is-not-null]]), while
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-q-covered-by-intervals-of-small-total-length.md-1668-  every at most countable set is ([[lem-countable-sets-are-null]]) and so is the
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-q-covered-by-intervals-of-small-total-length.md-1669-  uncountable Cantor set ([[thm-cantor-set-properties]]). The three facts
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-q-covered-by-intervals-of-small-total-length.md-1670-  together are what make the notion worth having.
