research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-fat-cantor-measure-computed.md-82-1.1 **Stage $n$.** By [L1] the intervals removed at stage $n$ are the $M^{(n)}_j$ for $j < N_n$, each of length $4^{-n-1}$, so their lengths total $\sum_{j<N_n} 4^{-n-1} = 2^{n} \cdot 4^{-n-1}$, which equals $4^{-1} \cdot 2^{-n}$ because $4^{-n-1} = 4^{-1} \cdot 4^{-n} = 4^{-1} \cdot 2^{-2n}$ and $2^{n} \cdot 2^{-2n} = 2^{-n}$ by [L1] and [L5]. [given, L1, L5]
