research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-fat-cantor-measure-computed.md-1345-**Closed intervals lose nothing.** A bounded interval with endpoints
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-fat-cantor-measure-computed.md-1346-$a \le b$ is contained in $[a,b]$ and has the same length ([[def-interval]]), so
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-fat-cantor-measure-computed.md-1347-a cover by intervals of any of the four bounded forms yields a cover by closed
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-fat-cantor-measure-computed.md-1348-intervals with the same lengths. The definition is therefore stated with closed
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-fat-cantor-measure-computed.md-1349-intervals once and for all. Covers by *open* intervals are a genuinely different
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-fat-cantor-measure-computed.md-1350-demand, and passing to one costs a little extra length: the enlargement
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-fat-cantor-measure-computed.md-1351-$[a_k,b_k] \subseteq (a_k - \delta_k,\ b_k + \delta_k)$ is carried out where it is
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-fat-cantor-measure-computed.md:1352:needed, in [[lem-nondegenerate-interval-is-not-null]] and in
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-fat-cantor-measure-computed.md-1353-[[thm-compact-null-is-content-zero]].
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-fat-cantor-measure-computed.md-1354-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-fat-cantor-measure-computed.md-1355-**Both notions are inherited by subsets.** If $B \subseteq A$ and $A$ is null,
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-fat-cantor-measure-computed.md-1356-then any cover of $A$ covers $B$, so $B$ is null; the same sentence with finite
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-fat-cantor-measure-computed.md-1357-covers shows a subset of a set of content zero has content zero.
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-fat-cantor-measure-computed.md-1358-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-fat-cantor-measure-computed.md-1359-**A finite cover is a countable cover, so content zero implies measure zero.**
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/ex-fat-cantor-measure-computed.md-1360-Padding the list $[a_0,b_0], \dots, [a_n,b_n]$ with the degenerate intervals
