research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/fs-nowhere-dense-implies-measure-zero.md-601-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/fs-nowhere-dense-implies-measure-zero.md-602-**Closed intervals lose nothing.** A bounded interval with endpoints
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/fs-nowhere-dense-implies-measure-zero.md-603-$a \le b$ is contained in $[a,b]$ and has the same length ([[def-interval]]), so
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/fs-nowhere-dense-implies-measure-zero.md-604-a cover by intervals of any of the four bounded forms yields a cover by closed
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/fs-nowhere-dense-implies-measure-zero.md-605-intervals with the same lengths. The definition is therefore stated with closed
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/fs-nowhere-dense-implies-measure-zero.md-606-intervals once and for all. Covers by *open* intervals are a genuinely different
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/fs-nowhere-dense-implies-measure-zero.md-607-demand, and passing to one costs a little extra length: the enlargement
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/fs-nowhere-dense-implies-measure-zero.md-608-$[a_k,b_k] \subseteq (a_k - \delta_k,\ b_k + \delta_k)$ is carried out where it is
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/fs-nowhere-dense-implies-measure-zero.md:609:needed, in [[lem-nondegenerate-interval-is-not-null]] and in
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/fs-nowhere-dense-implies-measure-zero.md-610-[[thm-compact-null-is-content-zero]].
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/fs-nowhere-dense-implies-measure-zero.md-611-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/fs-nowhere-dense-implies-measure-zero.md-612-**Both notions are inherited by subsets.** If $B \subseteq A$ and $A$ is null,
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/fs-nowhere-dense-implies-measure-zero.md-613-then any cover of $A$ covers $B$, so $B$ is null; the same sentence with finite
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/fs-nowhere-dense-implies-measure-zero.md-614-covers shows a subset of a set of content zero has content zero.
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/fs-nowhere-dense-implies-measure-zero.md-615-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/fs-nowhere-dense-implies-measure-zero.md-616-**A finite cover is a countable cover, so content zero implies measure zero.**
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/fs-nowhere-dense-implies-measure-zero.md-617-Padding the list $[a_0,b_0], \dots, [a_n,b_n]$ with the degenerate intervals
