research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cex-nowhere-dense-with-positive-measure.md-842-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cex-nowhere-dense-with-positive-measure.md-843-1.1 **Stage $n$.** By [L1] the intervals removed at stage $n$ are the $M^{(n)}_j$ for $j < N_n$, each of length $4^{-n-1}$, so their lengths total $\sum_{j<N_n} 4^{-n-1} = 2^{n} \cdot 4^{-n-1}$, which equals $4^{-1} \cdot 2^{-n}$ because $4^{-n-1} = 4^{-1} \cdot 4^{-n} = 4^{-1} \cdot 2^{-2n}$ and $2^{n} \cdot 2^{-2n} = 2^{-n}$ by [L1] and [L5]. [given, L1, L5]
--
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cex-nowhere-dense-with-positive-measure.md-945-  reason: $\mathbb{Q}$ has measure zero and is not nowhere dense
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cex-nowhere-dense-with-positive-measure.md-946-  ([[fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense]]). So neither of the two notions of
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cex-nowhere-dense-with-positive-measure.md-947-  smallness implies the other, and the two failures are witnessed by sets of
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cex-nowhere-dense-with-positive-measure.md-948-  different cardinality, $S$ being uncountable and $\mathbb{Q}$ countable.
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cex-nowhere-dense-with-positive-measure.md-949-
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cex-nowhere-dense-with-positive-measure.md-950-- **What is true.** A nowhere dense set contains no interval of positive length,
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cex-nowhere-dense-with-positive-measure.md-951-  which is a genuine consequence of the definition; and a set of measure zero
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cex-nowhere-dense-with-positive-measure.md-952-  also contains no interval of positive length
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cex-nowhere-dense-with-positive-measure.md:953:  ([[lem-nondegenerate-interval-is-not-null]]). The two conditions share that
research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cex-nowhere-dense-with-positive-measure.md-954-  consequence and nothing beyond it.
