research/audit/wave8-refuter-tasks/cex-nowhere-dense-with-positive-measure.md:1154:[L5] If $[u,v] \subseteq \bigcup_k [c_k,d_k]$ with $u \le v$, $c_k \le d_k$ and $\sum_{k<i}(d_k - c_k) \le M'$ for every $i$, then $M' \ge v - u$ ([[lem-nondegenerate-interval-is-not-null]]).
