research/audit/wave8-proof-contracts.json-12714-          "quote": "Let $A \\subseteq \\mathbb{R}$, with closure $\\overline{A}$ as in [[def-interior-closure-boundary-r]] and derived set $A'$ as in [[def-limit-point-r]]. Write $$E \\;:=\\; \\{\\, x \\in \\mathbb{R} : N_\\varepsilon(x) \\cap A \\ne \\varnothing \\text{ for every real } \\varepsilon > 0 \\,\\}$$ for the set of adherent points of $A$ ([[def-neighbourhood-r]]). Then: 1. $\\overline{A} = E$. 2. $\\overline{A} = A \\cup A'$. 3. $\\overline{A}$ is the smallest closed superset of $A$: it is closed, it contains $A$, and it is contained in every closed $F$ with $A \\subseteq F$. 4. $A$ is closed if and only if $A = \\overline{A}$, if and only if $A' \\subseteq A$. Claim 3 is the content of the definition of $\\overline{A}$ and is restated here so that the four descriptions stand together; claims 1, 2 and 4 are the ones that carry work.",
