research/audit/wave8-proof-contracts.json-15199-          "quote": "**The same bound holds for a cover by bounded intervals of any of the four bounded forms**, since an interval with endpoints $c \\le d$ is contained in $[c,d]$ and has the same length $d - c$ ([[def-interval]]); replacing each covering interval by the closed interval on its endpoints changes no length and only enlarges the union. In particular a finite family of intervals of total length strictly below $b - a$ cannot cover $[a,b]$, which is the form in which this lemma is used throughout the page.",
