research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-1101-
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-1102-**Closed intervals lose nothing.** A bounded interval with endpoints
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-1103-$a \le b$ is contained in $[a,b]$ and has the same length ([[def-interval]]), so
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-1104-a cover by intervals of any of the four bounded forms yields a cover by closed
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-1105-intervals with the same lengths. The definition is therefore stated with closed
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-1106-intervals once and for all. Covers by *open* intervals are a genuinely different
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-1107-demand, and passing to one costs a little extra length: the enlargement
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-1108-$[a_k,b_k] \subseteq (a_k - \delta_k,\ b_k + \delta_k)$ is carried out where it is
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md:1109:needed, in [[lem-nondegenerate-interval-is-not-null]] and in
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-1110-[[thm-compact-null-is-content-zero]].
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-1111-
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-1112-**Both notions are inherited by subsets.** If $B \subseteq A$ and $A$ is null,
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-1113-then any cover of $A$ covers $B$, so $B$ is null; the same sentence with finite
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-1114-covers shows a subset of a set of content zero has content zero.
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-1115-
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-1116-**A finite cover is a countable cover, so content zero implies measure zero.**
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-1117-Padding the list $[a_0,b_0], \dots, [a_n,b_n]$ with the degenerate intervals
--
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-1134-  notion is the vanishing of the Lebesgue outer measure. Neither outer quantity
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-1135-  is defined in this library, and no item here assigns a nonzero size to any set:
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-1136-  every statement is of the shape "can, or cannot, be covered by intervals of
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-1137-  total length below such and such a bound". That is a deliberate restriction of
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-1138-  scope at this point in the reading order, not a claim that the general notions
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-1139-  are unavailable in mathematics.
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-1140-
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-1141-- **Measure zero is not vacuous and not universal.** No interval with two
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md:1142:  distinct endpoints is null ([[lem-nondegenerate-interval-is-not-null]]), while
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-1143-  every at most countable set is ([[lem-countable-sets-are-null]]) and so is the
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-1144-  uncountable Cantor set ([[thm-cantor-set-properties]]). The three facts
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-1145-  together are what make the notion worth having.
