research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-1490-  reason: $\mathbb{Q}$ has measure zero and is not nowhere dense
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-1491-  ([[fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense]]). So neither of the two notions of
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-1492-  smallness implies the other, and the two failures are witnessed by sets of
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-1493-  different cardinality, $S$ being uncountable and $\mathbb{Q}$ countable.
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-1494-
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-1495-- **What is true.** A nowhere dense set contains no interval of positive length,
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-1496-  which is a genuine consequence of the definition; and a set of measure zero
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-1497-  also contains no interval of positive length
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md:1498:  ([[lem-nondegenerate-interval-is-not-null]]). The two conditions share that
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense.prompt.md-1499-  consequence and nothing beyond it.
