research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-thm-cantor-set-properties.prompt.md-156-[L3] $[c,d]$ is a closed set and a bounded interval, $(c,d)$ is open, $N_\varepsilon(x) = (x-\varepsilon, x+\varepsilon)$, and every open set contains a neighbourhood of each of its points ([[def-interval]], [[def-open-and-closed-in-r]], [[def-neighbourhood-r]]).
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-thm-cantor-set-properties.prompt.md-157-
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-thm-cantor-set-properties.prompt.md-158-[L4] Finite unions of closed sets are closed, and an intersection of a nonempty family of closed sets is closed ([[thm-open-set-algebra-r]]).
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-thm-cantor-set-properties.prompt.md-159-
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-thm-cantor-set-properties.prompt.md-160-[L5] A subset of $\mathbb{R}$ is compact exactly when it is closed and bounded ([[thm-heine-borel-characterisation-r]], [[def-open-cover-r]]).
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-thm-cantor-set-properties.prompt.md-161-
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-thm-cantor-set-properties.prompt.md:162:[L6] Content zero and measure zero as in [[def-measure-zero-and-content-zero]]; a set of content zero is null ([[lem-content-zero-implies-null]]); no null set contains an interval $[u,v]$ with $u < v$ ([[lem-nondegenerate-interval-is-not-null]]).
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-thm-cantor-set-properties.prompt.md-163-
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-thm-cantor-set-properties.prompt.md-164-[L7] $P$ is perfect when it is closed and no point of it is isolated in it ([[def-perfect-set-r]], [[def-limit-point-r]]); every nonempty perfect subset of $\mathbb{R}$ is uncountable ([[thm-perfect-set-uncountable-r]], [[def-countable]]).
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-thm-cantor-set-properties.prompt.md-165-
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-thm-cantor-set-properties.prompt.md-166-[L8] A set is nowhere dense exactly when the interior of its closure is empty, and a closed set equals its closure ([[def-nowhere-dense-meager]], [[def-interior-closure-boundary-r]], [[thm-closure-characterisations-r]]).
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-thm-cantor-set-properties.prompt.md-167-
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-thm-cantor-set-properties.prompt.md-168-[L9] A subset of $\mathbb{R}$ is connected exactly when it is order-convex ([[thm-connected-subsets-of-r-are-intervals]], [[def-connected-r]], [[def-interval]]).
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-thm-cantor-set-properties.prompt.md-169-
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-refuter-thm-cantor-set-properties.prompt.md-170-[L10] $|r|^k \to 0$ for $|r| < 1$ ([[lem-geometric-sequence-null]]); convergence to $0$ is tested against rational $\varepsilon > 0$ ([[def-real-limit]]); $|z| \ge 0$, $|z| = z$ for $z \ge 0$, and $|uv| = |u||v|$ ([[lem-of-abs-value]]).
