research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-cantor-continuity-A4.log-287801- {"id":"fs-nowhere-dense-implies-measure-zero","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.uchicago.edu/~may/REU2021/REUPapers/Jin%2CAlexa.pdf"],"rationale":"The fat Cantor source supplies the standard nowhere-dense positive-measure counterexample. The false claim and its local refutation are a dependency-level restatement of that counterexample.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-cantor-continuity-A4.log-287802- {"id":"fs-measure-zero-implies-nowhere-dense","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Analysis/Mathematical_Analysis_%28Zakon%29/06%3A_Differentiation_on_E_and_Other_Normed_Linear_Spaces/6.08%3A_Baire_Categories._More_on_Linear_Maps","https://math.mit.edu/classes/18.125/HW2.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources together record that the rationals are dense and countable, hence null but not nowhere dense. The local false statement is refuted by exactly that standard witness.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-cantor-continuity-A4.log-287803--{"id":"fs-null-implies-content-zero","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.mit.edu/classes/18.125/HW2.pdf","https://math.mit.edu/~brubaker/103PSet1Sol.pdf"],"rationale":"The MIT sources distinguish countable null covers from finite compact covers; the local bounded-rational witness is the direct failure of the converse without compactness.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
