research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-cantor-continuity-A4.log-301870--  notions may be used interchangeably, and the finite form is the one that
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-cantor-continuity-A4.log-301871--  combines with [[lem-finite-interval-cover-total-length]].
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-cantor-continuity-A4.log-301872-+- **The theorem is what makes content zero usable at all.** Every set to which content zero is applied on this page is compact: the Cantor set ([[thm-cantor-set-properties]]) and the Smith-Volterra-Cantor set ([[def-fat-cantor-set]]) are both closed and bounded, so for them the two notions may be used interchangeably, and the finite form is the one that combines with [[lem-finite-interval-cover-total-length]].
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-cantor-continuity-A4.log-301873- 
research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-cantor-continuity-A4.log-301874--- **The cost of opening up the cover is $\varepsilon \cdot 2^{-1}$, chosen in
