research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-cantor-continuity-A4.log:303091:+{"id":"lem-nondegenerate-interval-is-not-null","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://www.cs.uaf.edu/~maxwell/AY2007/math641/Measure.pdf"],"rationale":"The UAF notes give the countable interval-cover argument showing that an interval of positive length is not null, using compactness to pass to a finite subcover. The local proof follows that argument with this library’s series indexing.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
