research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-cantor-continuity-A4.log-311289- {"id":"def-nowhere-dense-meager","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Analysis/Mathematical_Analysis_%28Zakon%29/06%3A_Differentiation_on_E_and_Other_Normed_Linear_Spaces/6.08%3A_Baire_Categories._More_on_Linear_Maps","https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Meager_set"],"rationale":"Zakon and the Encyclopedia of Mathematics give the closure-interior definition of nowhere dense and the countable-union definition of meager. The local item also fixes residual and the second-category convention, so it is a bundled semantic restatement.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
