research/audit/wave8-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-cantor-continuity-A4.log-316766--{"id":"def-measure-zero-and-content-zero","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.mit.edu/classes/18.125/HW2.pdf","https://math.mit.edu/~brubaker/103PSet1Sol.pdf"],"rationale":"The MIT materials use the same epsilon-small countable interval-cover definition of nullity and contrast finite covers for compact null sets. The local term content zero is a deliberately elementary finite-cover convention, so the package is a semantic restatement rather than an exact quotation of Jordan measure.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
